Hanuman honoured by rakshasas enters Lanka and Ravana abode --- Hanuman bows and delivers Rama welfare and victory message --- Hanuman declares Ravana slain bridge built vow fulfilled and Lanka given to Vibhishana --- Sita leaps joy-bound speechless hearing beloved victory --- Sita says no gold jewels or kingdom equals reward for news --- Hanuman praises her sweet worthy speech and gained heaven seeing victorious Rama --- Hanuman begs leave to kill rakshasis tormenting her in Ashoka grove with fists feet teeth --- Sita forbids anger at obedient servant maids and blames fate and own karma --- Sita cites bear tiger verse to spare sinners and show compassion as ornament --- Hanuman praises her as Rama worthy wife and she asks to see husband and he promises sight of moon-faced Rama with Lakshmana